{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 2800,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- What will happen tomorrow is not random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5060,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, it's at least somewhat predictable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7540,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, not entirely to be sure, but some\nthings will happen for certain, and other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11680,
    "dDurationMs": 1570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "things definitely won't."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13250,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, the sun will rise, water will\nstill freeze at zero degrees celsius,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17670,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- and you won't become Michael Stevens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19990,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We know this because everything in the universe\nis made of 12 fundamental particles, and they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24160,
    "dDurationMs": 2759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "interact in four predictable ways."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26919,
    "dDurationMs": 5141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- What if I were able to determine the positions\nand velocities of every single one of these"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32060,
    "dDurationMs": 1189,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "particles in the universe?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33249,
    "dDurationMs": 4681,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Well, you would be the intelligence envisioned\nby Laplace, who thought if you could really"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37930,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "figure out where everything is and how fast\nit's moving, you would know the entire future"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42190,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the universe, because you know how every\nparticle interacts with every other particle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45230,
    "dDurationMs": 5250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Wow, so nothing would be unpredictable,\nwhich means, nothing would be random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50480,
    "dDurationMs": 2099,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Not even human behavior."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52579,
    "dDurationMs": 3512,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since we are made of the same fundamental\nparticles as everything in the rest of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56091,
    "dDurationMs": 6378,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "universe, everything we will ever do, or have\never done, would be determined by the information"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62469,
    "dDurationMs": 3211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the state of the universe at any one time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65680,
    "dDurationMs": 1610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But what is information?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67290,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, it seems to be fundamentally about order."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71170,
    "dDurationMs": 5490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The order of molecules in your DNA contain\nthe information needed to make you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76660,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is the order of zeros and ones streaming\nthrough the internet that contain all the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80710,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "information required to play this video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83020,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is the order of letters that makes a word,\nand the order of words that makes a sentence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86840,
    "dDurationMs": 1610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that carries information."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88450,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So fundamentally, information seems to be\nabout order."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93080,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Regularity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94280,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, until you really think about it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96880,
    "dDurationMs": 5690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, does every letter of a word carry\nthe same amount of information?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102570,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103570,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, after a \"Q\", you know almost for certain\nthat the next letter will be a \"U\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109330,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After a \"Th\", there will probably be an \"E\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112420,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So these letters carry very little information,\nbecause you could predict them beforehand."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116320,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are redundant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117640,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, the founder of information theory,\nClaude Shannon, estimated the redundancy of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122170,
    "dDurationMs": 6920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "English at about 75%, which is why we can\nmake sense of things like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129090,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So English can be compressed, because it is\nnot random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133200,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It has patterns."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134200,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, this video is compressible because\nof its regularities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138220,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In each frame, the pixels of similar color\ncluster together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141770,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Plus, from frame to frame, most of the pixels\ndon't change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145970,
    "dDurationMs": 3579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you only need to record the ones that do\nchange."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149549,
    "dDurationMs": 5611,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You can take advantage of this technique\nto create some trippy effects known as datamoshing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155160,
    "dDurationMs": 5930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the application of the movement data\nfrom one video, to the pixels of another."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161090,
    "dDurationMs": 3790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It also means that an average video can\nbe compressed to just one thousandth of its"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164880,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "original size."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166590,
    "dDurationMs": 2930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But what is the most you can compress something?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169520,
    "dDurationMs": 5290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Well, anything that is not random, any patters\nor regularities, can be reduced, because they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174810,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are predictable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176150,
    "dDurationMs": 6559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can continue shrinking a file down\nuntil what you're left with is totally random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182709,
    "dDurationMs": 5971,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And that will contain all of the information\nof the original item but distilled."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188680,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pure information."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191080,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So pure information is randomness."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195630,
    "dDurationMs": 6189,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to know how much information something\ncontains, you need to know how random it is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201819,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And randomness is disorder..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204319,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What we also call ..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205319,
    "dDurationMs": 2781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Both] Entropy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208100,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So information, fundamentally, is entropy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212030,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This makes sense if you consider a string\nof binary digits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215120,
    "dDurationMs": 2949,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, this string is perfectly ordered."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218069,
    "dDurationMs": 3631,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It has very low entropy, and it contains no\ninformation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221700,
    "dDurationMs": 1899,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's the state of an erased hard drive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223599,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this string contains slightly more information,\nbut again, the regularities allow it to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228069,
    "dDurationMs": 1651,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "easily compressed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229720,
    "dDurationMs": 7060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the string that contains the maximum amount\nof information is just-- a random set of zeros"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236780,
    "dDurationMs": 1990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and ones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238770,
    "dDurationMs": 2870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It has maximum entropy because it's totally\ndisordered."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241640,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You could not predict any of those digits\nby looking at any of the other digits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246110,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you wanted to send this information\nto someone, you would have no other option"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250360,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but to send the whole string of digits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252310,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's no way to compress it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255010,
    "dDurationMs": 4199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But here's the thing about any object that\ncontains maximum information."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259209,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For us as human beings, they carry no meaning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262419,
    "dDurationMs": 4291,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, a video containing maximum information\nwould look like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 266710,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is just white noise."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269990,
    "dDurationMs": 4399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The color of each pixel is independent of\nall the other pixels, and they all change"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274389,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "randomly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275389,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This video could not be compressed, because\nit's already totally random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278699,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now a random sequence of DNA would not make\nan organism."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282809,
    "dDurationMs": 4551,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And a random string of letters does not generally\nmake a word."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287360,
    "dDurationMs": 5169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We are drawn to things that are neither perfectly\nordered, containing no information, nor are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292529,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they perfectly disordered, containing maximum\ninformation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296729,
    "dDurationMs": 5870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Somewhere in the middle, we can recognize\ncomplex patterns, and that is where we derive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302599,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303599,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In music, poetry, and ideas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305779,
    "dDurationMs": 6531,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is this search for meaning that leads us\nto propose scientific theories, which if you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312310,
    "dDurationMs": 3779,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "think about it, are really our way of compressing\nthe universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316089,
    "dDurationMs": 5050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, general relativity, our current\ntheory of gravity, compresses into one short"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321139,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "equation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322259,
    "dDurationMs": 3701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everything from how an apple falls to the\nearth, to how the moon orbits the earth, how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325960,
    "dDurationMs": 4419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all the planets orbit the sun, how the sun\norbits a supermassive blackhole at the center"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330379,
    "dDurationMs": 5331,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of our galaxy, how blackholes form and behave,\nand how the whole universe expands out from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335710,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Big Bang."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338370,
    "dDurationMs": 2859,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now that we have this theory, the future is\nmore predictable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341229,
    "dDurationMs": 4021,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, we can predict eclipses thousands\nof years into the future."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345250,
    "dDurationMs": 5289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, with all of our scientific theories, does\nthat mean that the universe is completely"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350539,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not random?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352379,
    "dDurationMs": 2141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That it is perfectly predictable?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354520,
    "dDurationMs": 4291,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, let's assume for a second that Laplace\nwas right, and that knowing the state of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358811,
    "dDurationMs": 5559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "universe at any one time, means you also know\nits state at every other time as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364370,
    "dDurationMs": 5150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, that would mean that the information\nin our universe would be constant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369520,
    "dDurationMs": 7760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if information is entropy, that would\nmean the entropy of the universe is also constant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377280,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that does not appear to be the universe\nthat we live in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380550,
    "dDurationMs": 5250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The second law of thermodynamics states that\nentropy in the universe increases with time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385800,
    "dDurationMs": 3299,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or in other words, things don't stir themselves\napart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389099,
    "dDurationMs": 4391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if entropy is going up, that means the\ninformation in our universe is constantly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393490,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "increasing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394840,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That makes sense, because it would take more\ninformation to specify the state of the universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398800,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now, than right after the Big Bang."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401110,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, where is this new information coming from?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404930,
    "dDurationMs": 3139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "My best bet is quantum mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408069,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Quantum mechanics describes how the 12 fundamental\nparticles behave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411909,
    "dDurationMs": 5850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as spectacularly successful as it is,\nit is only a probabilistic theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417759,
    "dDurationMs": 4231,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meaning that you cannot predict with absolute\ncertainty where an electron, say, will be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421990,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at some later time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423750,
    "dDurationMs": 4409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can only calculate probabilities of where\nyou are likely to find it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428159,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when you do interact with it, and locate\nthe electron at a particular point, you have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432779,
    "dDurationMs": 1850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gained information."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434629,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You now know something that you couldn't have\npredicted with certainty beforehand."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439219,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This drove Einstein crazy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440749,
    "dDurationMs": 3411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He said, \"God does not play dice,\" referring\nto this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444160,
    "dDurationMs": 4879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, he wished that we could compress our\ntheory of quantum mechanics further, so that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449039,
    "dDurationMs": 4231,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we could really figure out where these particles\nwere going to be."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453270,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But maybe the reason why we haven't been able\nto compress quantum mechanics further, is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457030,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because fundamentally, it's random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460340,
    "dDurationMs": 7949,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fundamentally, new information is being generated\nevery time a quantum event like that occurs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468289,
    "dDurationMs": 7340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In that case, it could be these quantum measurements\nwhich are driving up the entropy of the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475629,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are creating new information all of the\ntime, and that means the disorder in our universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480089,
    "dDurationMs": 1181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "must go up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481270,
    "dDurationMs": 4299,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is what we observe as the second law\nof thermodynamics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 485569,
    "dDurationMs": 3141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, we often think about the second\nlaw as a curse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488710,
    "dDurationMs": 4819,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As though everything which is ordered is going\ntowards disorder."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493529,
    "dDurationMs": 6980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But maybe, I mean, it's only in a universe\nwhere this law is obeyed, that the truly unexpected"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500509,
    "dDurationMs": 1451,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can occur."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501960,
    "dDurationMs": 4289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That the future can be actually undetermined."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506249,
    "dDurationMs": 6141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For us really to have free will, we need the\nsecond law of thermodynamics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512390,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, you might think that these quantum events\nare too small to have any meaningful impact"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517130,
    "dDurationMs": 3529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the evolution of the universe, but that\nis not true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 520659,
    "dDurationMs": 4901,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's because, there are physical systems\nwhich are so dependent, so sensitive to the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525560,
    "dDurationMs": 6540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "initial conditions that any tiny change will\nend up making a big difference later down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 532100,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the track."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533360,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's called \"chaos.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535260,
    "dDurationMs": 3059,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it's also known as \"the butterfly effect.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538319,
    "dDurationMs": 2871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you and I could be such physical systems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541190,
    "dDurationMs": 1070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chaotic systems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542260,
    "dDurationMs": 10800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And our free will could come from quantum\nevents in our brains."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553060,
    "dDurationMs": 3370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it looks as though we live in a universe\nwhere the future is yet to be determined."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556430,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is to say, it is at least somewhat random."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559310,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- But Derek, what is the most random thing\npossible in the universe?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563250,
    "dDurationMs": 1930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That's a good question, Michael."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565180,
    "dDurationMs": 4719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- You know, it's such a good question, I'm\ntalking about it over on Vsauce."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569899,
    "dDurationMs": 2350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do you wanna go find out about randomness\nwith me?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572249,
    "dDurationMs": 1130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Let's go check it out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 573379,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Alright."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574379,
    "dDurationMs": 2710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- And you can decide whether to click over\nor not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577089,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Oh, that's nice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578589,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579589,
    "dDurationMs": 1,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah."
    } ]
  } ]
}
